{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2451","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2451","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2451\",\"parent_revision\":\"065ac562d7d64a2e37408fbfd3e432830268f3c9a845fb345557510b79732297\",\"root_revision\":\"065ac562d7d64a2e37408fbfd3e432830268f3c9a845fb345557510b79732297\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe sam_plan(action='read') MCP tool response includes a source_path field containing the filesystem path to the plan's local YAML storage file (e.g. /home/user/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/P2057d4e0-slug.yaml). This exposes a local_yaml backend implementation detail through the public MCP surface.\\n\\nInvestigation confirmed (2026-05-24):\\n- source_path is output-only \u2014 zero callers pass it as input to any SAM tool\\n- plan-validator.md:482 explicitly prohibits agents from using it: \\\"Do NOT attempt to read the file at the literal path \u2014 extract the plan ID and use sam_plan\\\"\\n- All other backends (memory, beads, github_task) return None for this field\\n- plan_dir is the legitimate path-taking parameter and identifies a directory, not a plan file\\n\\nThe field is declared in PlanData, PlanSummary, and PlanFieldsUpdate TypedDicts but no MCP tool signature accepts it as input. It provides no value to consuming agents and creates a coupling temptation \u2014 an agent that sees a filesystem path may bypass the MCP abstraction and attempt direct file access.\\n\\nRemediation options (from research report at .tmp/scratch/reports/sam-yaml-path-research.md):\\n1. Remove source_path from public TypedDicts entirely\\n2. Split read/write TypedDicts so source_path only appears in internal shapes\\n3. Rename to _source_path and document as backend-internal debug field\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll claims verified against primary sources (2026-05-28):\\n\\n- **source_path is output-only (zero callers pass it as input)**: VERIFIED \u2014 grep across all backends, server.py, and tests shows `source_path` is only SET in backend response dicts, never read from incoming config/input. `PlanFieldsUpdate` includes it but no test or call site passes it in an update payload.\\n- **plan-validator.md:482 prohibits use of the path**: VERIFIED \u2014 line 482 reads: \\\"Do NOT attempt to read the file at the literal path \u2014 it is not repo-relative.\\\"\\n- **All other backends return None**: VERIFIED \u2014 memory.py:256, beads.py:244/599/725, github_task.py:341/359/384 all set `source_path: None`.\\n- **Field declared in PlanData, PlanSummary, PlanFieldsUpdate**: VERIFIED \u2014 task_backend_types.py lines 119, 217, 153.\\n- **No MCP tool signature accepts it as input**: VERIFIED \u2014 server.py tool signatures do not expose source_path as a parameter.\\n- **Internal use exists**: VERIFIED \u2014 server.py:319 reads `plan_data[\\\"source_path\\\"]` for artifact registration; query.py:267\u2013270 derives plan_id stem; local_yaml.py:279\u2013282 uses it for write routing.\\n- **Test file references**: VERIFIED \u2014 plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py lines 62, 100, 138 contain source_path in mock data.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **MCP public surface**: `sam_plan(action='read')` and `sam_plan(action='list')` responses currently expose `source_path` containing a filesystem path only meaningful on the machine running the local_yaml backend.\\n- **Coupling temptation**: Any agent receiving a filesystem path may attempt direct file access (`Read(file_path=source_path)`), bypassing the MCP abstraction. `plan-validator.md:482` explicitly prohibits this pattern.\\n- **Backend portability**: Three of four backends (memory, beads, github_task) return `None` for `source_path`. Agent code that branches on `source_path` being present silently breaks on non-local backends.\\n- **`PlanFieldsUpdate` inclusion**: `source_path` in the update TypedDict implies agents could attempt to write it as a mutable field \u2014 semantically wrong since it is a storage artefact, not a plan property.\\n- **Internal use exists**: `server.py:319\u2013320` reads `plan_data[\\\"source_path\\\"]` to trigger artifact registration. `local_yaml.py:279\u2013282` uses `plan.source_path` for write routing. `query.py:267\u2013270` derives plan number from it. These internal usages must survive the refactor but do not require the field in the public MCP response.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Removes a backend-specific implementation detail from the public MCP contract, making responses backend-agnostic.\\n- Eliminates a class of agent misbehavior where agents attempt direct filesystem access using the exposed path.\\n- Improves type clarity: splitting internal backend shapes from public MCP response shapes makes the boundary explicit in the type system.\\n- `PlanFieldsUpdate` no longer accepts a field with no semantic meaning as a plan property.\\n- All non-local backends (memory, beads, github_task) currently return `None` for a field annotated as required in `TypedDict` \u2014 removing it eliminates a type contract violation for those backends.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter the fix, `sam_plan(action='read')` and `sam_plan(action='list')` responses must not contain a `source_path` key. The MCP tool continues to function correctly. Plan identity, task data, goal, context, and all other fields remain present. Internal backend operations (artifact registration, plan-ID derivation, YAML write routing) continue to use the filesystem path via internal shapes that do not flow to the MCP response.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target state:\\n\\n1. `PlanData` TypedDict (public MCP response shape for `read_plan`) does not contain `source_path`.\\n2. `PlanSummary` TypedDict (public MCP response shape for `list_plans`) does not contain `source_path`.\\n3. `PlanFieldsUpdate` TypedDict (input shape for `update_plan_fields`) does not contain `source_path`.\\n4. Internal backend operations that depend on `source_path` use an internal shape (e.g. a private `_InternalPlanData` TypedDict extending the public one with `source_path`) to pass the value without exposing it through the public type.\\n5. `Plan` Pydantic model in `models.py` may retain `source_path` as an internal field \u2014 it is the domain model, not the public contract.\\n6. All existing backend tests that assert `source_path` in mock data are updated to reflect the new shape.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/` exits 0 with no new errors after the change.\\n2. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/` exits 0 \u2014 all existing tests pass (or are updated to remove `source_path` assertions from mock data).\\n3. `sam_plan(action='read')` response serialised to JSON does not contain a `source_path` key.\\n4. `sam_plan(action='list')` response items serialised to JSON do not contain a `source_path` key.\\n5. `PlanData`, `PlanSummary`, and `PlanFieldsUpdate` TypedDicts in `task_backend_types.py` contain no `source_path` field after the change.\\n6. No `Any` or `object` type annotations are introduced.\\n7. The `server.py` artifact-registration path (currently `plan_data[\\\"source_path\\\"]` at line 319) continues to function \u2014 the path value must reach the registration call via the chosen internal mechanism.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend_types.py` \u2014 PlanData (line 119), PlanSummary (line 217), PlanFieldsUpdate (line 153) TypedDicts |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py` \u2014 only backend that sets non-None source_path; uses it at lines 155, 279\u2013282, 340 |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py` \u2014 sets `source_path: None` (lines 256, 301) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/beads.py` \u2014 sets `source_path: None` (lines 244, 599, 725) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py` \u2014 sets `source_path=None` (lines 341, 359, 384) |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/server.py` \u2014 reads `plan_data[\\\"source_path\\\"]` at line 319 for artifact registration |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py` \u2014 reads `plan.source_path` at lines 267\u2013270 to derive plan_id stem |\\n| Source file | `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Plan Pydantic model has `source_path: Path | None` at line 319 |\\n| Test file | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_server_sam_taskbackend.py` \u2014 mocks include `source_path` at lines 62, 100, 138; must be updated |\\n| Related item | #1775 \u2014 Replace AppendTaskConfig.task_yaml: str with typed TaskDefinition (same TypedDict boundary theme) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 standalone refactor with no prerequisite backlog items.\\n- Blocks: None identified. Item #1775 touches the same TypedDict boundary layer but has no ordering dependency with this item.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 change is contained to `task_backend_types.py` (TypedDict updates) plus mechanical updates to four backend files, `server.py`, and tests. The main design decision (which of the three remediation options to choose) is the only judgment call. Option 2 (split TypedDicts) requires introducing one new internal TypedDict; Options 1 and 3 require fewer lines. No new abstractions, no cross-cutting concerns.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\nAPPROVED-FOR-PLANNING. All inputs are present or derivable from the primary sources.\\n\\n- Functional intent: PRESENT \u2014 remove `source_path` from public TypedDict shapes so the local YAML backend implementation detail is not exposed via the MCP surface.\\n- Scope boundaries: PRESENT \u2014 change is bounded to `task_backend_types.py` TypedDicts plus mechanical updates to four backend files, `server.py`, and tests.\\n- External interfaces: PRESENT \u2014 the MCP tool signatures for `sam_plan` are the affected public surface; they are inspectable in `server.py`.\\n- Constraints: PRESENT \u2014 no `Any` or `object` type annotations may be introduced; TypedDicts must be used for type boundaries.\\n- Existing system context: PRESENT \u2014 all affected files confirmed in codebase via grep.\\n- Verification expectations: PRESENT \u2014 `uv run ty check` and `uv run pytest` commands are the quality gates.\\n\\nIssue classification: refactor \u2014 non-behavioural change to type boundary shapes.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor: remove source_path from sam_plan read response \u2014 local yaml backend path is an implementation leak** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 work-backlog-item #2437 planning 2026-05-24 + background research agent\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ff51984c8ce48932d54acf4c400ff6b5246a4cacdc9088854fc8be7e4575ba5a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTAkRw\"}"}